statement.paragraph:
Let $\mathbf{u}_{1} = {\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
    {- 2} \\
    4 \\
    {- 6}
    \end{array} \right\rbrack,}$ $\mathbf{u}_{2} = {\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
    1 \\
    2 \\
    {- 5}
    \end{array} \right\rbrack,}$ $\mathbf{b} = {\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
    b_{1} \\
    b_{2} \\
    b_{3}
    \end{array} \right\rbrack,}$ and $W = \text{Span~}\{\mathbf{u}_{1}\text{,~}\mathbf{u}_{2}\}$. Find an implicit description of $W$; that is, find a set of one or more homogeneous equations that characterize the points of $W$. [Hint:When is $\mathbf{b}$ in $W$?]
